=========================================================
🏆 TOURNAMENT LEADERBOARD APP - LOCAL SETUP GUIDE
=========================================================
Welcome to your Tournament Leaderboard App! This guide will 
walk you through exactly how to run this application on your 
own computer and how to manage your match data locally.

---------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1: INSTALL NODE.JS
---------------------------------------------------------
To run this application, your computer needs Node.js (the 
engine that runs the server).

1. Go to the official website: https://nodejs.org/
2. Download the "LTS" (Long Term Support) version.
3. Run the installer and follow the standard installation 
   prompts. Keep all default settings (make sure it installs 
   NPM alongside Node.js).
4. Restart your computer if prompted.

---------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2: OPEN THE PROJECT
---------------------------------------------------------
1. Unzip/extract this project folder anywhere on your computer.
2. Open a Terminal or Command Prompt:
   - On Windows: Open the project folder, click the address 
     bar at the top, type `cmd`, and press Enter.
   - On Mac: Open Terminal, type `cd ` (with a space), drag 
     the project folder into the terminal window, and press 
     Enter.

---------------------------------------------------------
STEP 3: INSTALL REQUIRED MODULES
---------------------------------------------------------
Before running the app for the first time, you need to 
download the project's dependencies (React, Express, etc.).

1. In your Terminal (making sure you are inside the project 
   folder), type the following command and press Enter:
   
   npm install

2. Wait for it to finish. It will create a "node_modules" 
   folder. You only need to do this step once!

---------------------------------------------------------
STEP 4: START THE SERVER
---------------------------------------------------------
To turn on your application:

1. In the same Terminal, type:
   
   npm run dev

2. Press Enter. You should see a message saying the server 
   is running on http://localhost:3000.
3. Keep this terminal window open! If you close it, the app 
   will turn off.

---------------------------------------------------------
STEP 5: OPEN THE APP IN YOUR BROWSER
---------------------------------------------------------
Open Chrome, Safari, or Edge and go to these links:

- Main Leaderboard: http://localhost:3000/
- Match Rankings:   http://localhost:3000/rankings
- Admin Panel:      http://localhost:3000/admin

(Tip: You can open the Admin panel on your phone or a 
second monitor if they are on the same WiFi network, using 
your computer's local IP address instead of "localhost"!)

---------------------------------------------------------
STEP 6: HOW TO MANAGE & SAVE MATCHES
---------------------------------------------------------
Because you are running this locally, all your data is 
safely saved directly to your hard drive. 

1. LIVE UPDATES: 
   Go to the Admin Panel. Change team names, adjust points, 
   or mark players as eliminated. The moment you make a 
   change, the `data.json` file in your project folder is 
   automatically updated, and the Main Leaderboard will 
   animate the changes in real-time.

2. SAVING MATCH HISTORY:
   When a match is completely finished and you want to save 
   the final results before resetting for the next game:
   - Go to the Admin Panel.
   - Ensure the "DAY" and "MATCH" numbers at the top are correct.
   - Click the green "End Match & Save Data" button.
   
3. WHERE DOES IT SAVE?
   Clicking that button takes a snapshot of the current 
   scores and saves it permanently as a text file inside 
   the `data/matches/` folder in your project directory. 
   You can view these saved match results anytime in the 
   "Match History" tab of the Admin Panel!

4. RESETTING FOR THE NEXT GAME:
   After saving your match, you can click the red "Reset 
   Scores" button to wipe the live `data.json` board clean 
   for the next round. (Your saved match history will NOT 
   be deleted).

=========================================================
TROUBLESHOOTING
=========================================================
- "Command not found: npm" -> Node.js is not installed 
  correctly or you need to restart your terminal/computer.
- "Port 3000 is already in use" -> You already have a 
  terminal running the app. Close the old terminal, or press 
  Ctrl+C to stop the server before starting it again.
